WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.536
An OSINT workstation is a controlled environment for legitimate, organized,

00:00:04.536 --> 00:00:06.311
and repeatable public-source research.

00:00:06.311 --> 00:00:11.635
Separation from personal browsing reduces contamination and supports clear handling of settings,

00:00:11.635 --> 00:00:13.853
accounts, case files, and evidence.

00:00:13.853 --> 00:00:18.289
Design starts with investigation types, privacy rules, storage, browser workflows,

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:20.064
documentation, auditability, and recovery.

00:00:20.064 --> 00:00:24.500
Hardware and operating systems should be supported, reliable, and maintainable.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.936
Complexity is useful only when it solves a defined risk.

00:00:28.936 --> 00:00:33.373
Dedicated browser profiles, structured notes, source logs, timestamps, contextual captures,

00:00:33.373 --> 00:00:35.591
and raw-versus-analysis separation preserve traceability.

00:00:35.591 --> 00:00:40.027
Security depends on updates, strong authentication, endpoint protection, account separation,

00:00:40.027 --> 00:00:42.245
access limits, and ethical boundaries.

00:00:42.245 --> 00:00:45.351
Encrypted storage, tested backups, retention schedules, cleanup,

00:00:45.351 --> 00:00:49.344
and audit trails protect case material throughout its lifecycle.

00:00:49.344 --> 00:00:53.780
Tools should be selected for workflow value, security, data handling,

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:57.329
and export quality rather than popularity or novelty.

00:00:57.329 --> 00:01:03.096
The goal is disciplined intelligence work, not collecting tools or claiming perfect anonymity.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:07.533
A good workstation helps analysts answer scoped questions, validate evidence,

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:09.751
document reasoning, protect sensitive information,

00:01:09.751 --> 00:01:13.300
and report responsibly under organizational policy and law.
